    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711">

                <pb facs="0767" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.516 Export-Import Bank/733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-16T18:00:00-03:00">March 16, 1943—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1292. During Warren Pierson’s stay we have made encouraging progress on a
                    financing program for naturalization [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >nationalization</hi>] of Axis interests here. Agreement has been reached
                    with the Bank of Brazil on principles to be observed and with regard to
                    Export-Import Bank participation on a loan basis through the Bank of Brazil.
                    However, further negotiations with the Minister of Finance<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d711-f1"/> and General Portella, Chairman of the Economic Defense
                    Commission, are scheduled for the next week or 10 days. Pierson is leaving for
                    Lima <pb facs="0768" n="756" xml:id="pg756"/> March 19. He suggests, and I
                    agree, that Walmsley<anchor n="85" xml:id="d711-f2"/> stay here a few days
                    longer to cooperate with us in this work.</p>
                <p>If the Department approves, Pierson and Walmsley should reach Washington
                    approximately March 30.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
